# The list holds unboxed doubles. A push is inline: a test of the length against the capacity, the store of the element, one more on the length.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[fits]] = Below(b@[[length]], b@[[capacity]], {{*}}:HasSpareArrayCapacity)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[fits]], Terminal, {{*}}:HasSpareArrayCapacity)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[push]], Else:Rare:#
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[push]]:
# CHECK: Double b@[[element]] = IToD(b@[[k]],
# CHECK: Store(b@[[element]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:indexedDoubleProperties,
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[longer]] = Add(b@[[length]], $1(
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# The storage and its capacity are read ahead of the loop. Nothing in it calls, tests the kind of storage, or reads the list itself.
# NONE-LABEL: steps by 1
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSObject_butterfly
# NONE-NOT: Reads:Butterfly_vectorLength
# The length is a variable of the loop. The storage gets it where the loop is left.
# NONE-NOT: Butterfly_publicLength
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSCell
# NONE-NOT: :CallDirect
# The turns can be counted ahead of the loop: where they are few it goes without its poll, and a copy of it that polls takes the others.
# NONE-NOT: Patchpoint(
# NONE-LABEL: end of loop
# The list is made with room for all the elements, since the loop says how many there will be. Growing is out of the loop.
# CALLS: f1: size=
# The turn that has to grow the list ends in a copy of its own, and the loop goes on as before behind it.
# CALLS: operation operationAOTReserveArrayCapacity x2
# CALLS-NEXT: stub ArrayPush x4
# CALLS-NEXT: stub NewArrayWithLength.Double x1
# CALLS-NEXT: stub NewEmptyArray.DoubleDefaultCapacity x1
# CALLS-NOT: stub
# CALLS-NOT: operation
# CALLS: f{{*}}: size=
# Two of the seven are for the length: the test, the addition.
# Two of the rare nine, which run once in 1,048,576 turns, are the store in front of the poll and the read behind it.
# X64-NOT: , instructions:
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 7, patchpoints: 0
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 7, patchpoints: 0, rare instructions: 9, {{*}}entered rarely
# X64-NOT: , instructions:
# ARM64-NOT: , instructions:
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 6, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: {{*}}, patchpoints: 0, rare instructions: {{*}}entered rarely
# ARM64-NOT: , instructions:
# The length is read in front of the loop and stored where the loop ends.
# WAYS: Int32 b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_publicLength,
# WAYS: Int32 b@[[length]] = Phi(
# WAYS: Int32 b@[[longer]] = Add(b@[[length]], $1(
# WAYS: Store(b@[[longer]], b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Writes:Butterfly_publicLength,
# Where the list is full, perhaps nothing was pushed yet. Then nothing is stored: nobody may write to the storage of a literal.
# WAYS: Int32 b@[[stored]] = Load(b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_publicLength,
# WAYS-NEXT: Int32 b@[[differs]] = NotEqual(b@[[length]], b@[[stored]],
# WAYS-NEXT: Branch(b@[[differs]], Terminal,
# WAYS: Store(b@[[length]], b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Writes:Butterfly_publicLength,
# The copy of the loop that polls stores the length in front of the poll, where a collection may look at the list, and reads it again behind it.
# WAYS: Store(b@{{*}}, b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Writes:Butterfly_publicLength,
# WAYS: isLoopPoll
# WAYS: Load(b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_publicLength,
